  {
    "number": 54,
    "title": "Validate Pixoo reliability and support configured HTTP proxies",
    "body": "## Change\n\nRefs #12. The device transport created an HTTP agent that bypassed Node's enabled environment proxy, preventing the authorized Codex session from reaching the configured Pixoo. It now uses Node's configured route while retaining fresh connections, fixed device destinations, cancellation and the serialized writer. Node >=24.5 <25 is declared for standard HTTP proxy support.\n\nThe PR also records dated physical playback, controls, recovery, soak and variable-timing observations. This is a contract-preserving compatibility fix and evidence update; no OpenSpec delta or expanded application profile applies.\n\n## Validation\n\nAt candidate `74ffc2eb7af1af9c0fdc76246422dd3470a035e2` on Node 24.20.0:\n\n- `npm ci` and `npm run check` passed: 276 application tests across 40 files, 10 workflow tests, 12 specifications and 13 archives.\n- The proxy regression failed before the fix and passed afterward. It covers proxy opt-in, direct operation, NO_PROXY and separate connections.\n- Supplementary browser validation passed all 52 tests with installed Chromium149 headless shell, the repository assertions and a private executable/output override. Desktop/mobile playlist editor screenshots were inspected without a clear visual defect.\n- [PR run 34291316108](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/divoom-app-upgrade/actions/runs/34291316108), attempt 1, passed all five configured jobs: Workflow and Application on Linux/Windows, plus Simulator browser with the pinned Chromium. The run is associated with this PR/head and base `459968ef11a8fb4558b3c76411e14d4564d6929f`.\n\n## Review and remaining acceptance\n\nIndependent read-only Standards and Specification reviews inspected the same base/merge-base `459968ef11a8fb4558b3c76411e14d4564d6929f` and head `74ffc2eb7af1af9c0fdc76246422dd3470a035e2`. Neither found P0-P3 defects. Standards additionally checked cancellation through a stalled loopback proxy. Specification independently reconciled the physical logs and measurements.\n\nSpecification also confirmed that issue #12 is incomplete: effective variable timing was not demonstrated. No scope deferral has been accepted. The owner paused further visual testing and requested independent work continue. Keep this PR draft and the issue open; passing source reviews and CI do not satisfy that remaining hardware criterion. Main CI after an eventual merge and companion guide completion also remain required.\n\n## Runtime and hardware impact\n\nPhysical tests used application source `15b0820eaf14e6d61da44e299b2407f339bfe6c1`, the existing Pixoo64 smoke profile and one normal application writer through the approved proxy. Firmware is unknown. The owner confirmed controls, paused backend recovery and explicit Resume after a power interruption. Defect #52 owns accepted GIF-to-still flashing. Screen-on returning native GIFs is a separately accepted limitation with a verified explicit-Resume path.\n\nThe soak completed 60 minutes 2.192 seconds and 119 ordered transitions, with no backend error/recovery event and successful Stop/close. The owner confirmed continued alternation through the end with only known flashing. Backend loading median/p95/max were 246.307/379.620/1105.055 ms; median RSS rose 6.750 MiB between early and final sampling windows. The hardware document retains measurement definitions and limits.\n\nVisible blue dwell readings were about 28 seconds, then 30.3 seconds twice. Variable-stage A was uncertain, B looked equal despite different requested delays, and the equal-duration control looked equal. HTTP completion does not establish physical timing. The uniform-500-ms application profile is unchanged. All physical helpers are closed; final blue 30 was owner-confirmed. No further physical operation, installation or phone-access acceptance is claimed.\n\n## Cross-project work guide\n\n- [ ] Linked the coordinated hub guide PR and recorded its synchronization status.\n- [x] Updated the local acceptance narrative and maintenance history on the latest hub baseline, preserving the Pixoo #29 companion changes.\n- [ ] Completed final guide validation, independent review and required publication/merge gates. The companion remains in preparation; synchronization is unfinished.\n",
    "state": "open",
